cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use OpenMagic, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "OpenMagic: an AI coding toolbar for any web app"
abstract: >-
  OpenMagic is an open-source AI coding toolbar that injects into any running web
  application via a single-port reverse proxy. Select an element, describe a change
  in plain English, review the diff, and OpenMagic edits your real source code —
  then verifies the change (typecheck/lint + runtime) and self-corrects if it broke
  the build. Includes a visual element editor with live preview and a one-click
  AI UI/UX design review. Works across 14 LLM providers and 70+ models, bring your
  own key. No plugin, no IDE extension, no account.
type: software
authors:
